From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lusoris <lusoris@proton.me>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 20:54:47 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] avfilter/vf_tonemap_vaapi: add the bt2408_hable tone map

Add a tonemap option with the value bt2408_hable, which applies the
tone map of vf_tonemap through the VAAPI 3D LUT filter instead of the
driver's own curve. The filter fills the same FFBT2408Hable state as the
CPU filter, samples it on the PQ R'G'B' grid of the largest 16-bit RGB
3D LUT the driver offers, and uploads the table again when the peak or
the input primaries change. A driver without such a 3D LUT filter is
refused with an error; there is no fallback to the driver curve.

The table maps to 8-bit full range BT.709 RGB. With a YUV output format
the Intel media driver converts the table output once more and the
colours come out wrong, so the curve requires an 8-bit RGB output
format and defaults to rgba. A new peak option overrides the signal
peak taken from the side data.

On an Arc A380 with the iHD driver the output matches the CPU
tonemap=bt2408_hable path within one code value on flat test colours.
Against vf_libplacebo with tonemapping=hable the mean CIEDE2000 is 1.15
on four frames of a 720p Dolby Vision profile 5 clip through
dovi_reshape and 0.75 on ten frames of a 2160p HDR10 clip.

Signed-off-by: lusoris <lusoris@proton.me>
---
 doc/filters.texi               |  24 +++
 libavfilter/Makefile           |   2 +-
 libavfilter/vf_tonemap_vaapi.c | 270 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 3 files changed, 289 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/doc/filters.texi b/doc/filters.texi
index 4ef76ab4ae0421a98fdeca15cb0e14c28d23d66b..88505736fe1ce8aea06bc0f88c54843d646bdfb9 100644
--- a/doc/filters.texi
+++ b/doc/filters.texi
@@ -28878,12 +28878,36 @@ the maximum average light level.
 It is ignored for HDR-to-SDR tone-mapping, and optional for HDR-to-HDR
 tone-mapping.
 
+@item tonemap
+Set the tone map curve. By default the driver applies its own curve.
+
+@table @samp
+@item bt2408_hable
+Use the curve of @code{tonemap=bt2408_hable} (@pxref{tonemap}). The filter
+fills a 3D lookup table from it and the driver applies the table, so the
+driver must support the 3D LUT filter. The output is 8-bit full range RGB in
+BT.709 primaries and transfer, whatever @option{primaries}, @option{transfer}
+and @option{matrix} say; @option{format} must be an 8-bit RGB format such as
+@code{rgba} or @code{bgra} and defaults to @code{rgba}. The option
+@option{display} cannot be combined with this curve.
+@end table
+
+@item peak
+Override the signal peak for @code{tonemap=bt2408_hable}, in units of
+100 nits. Default is 0, which takes the peak from the frame side data.
+
 @end table
 
 @subsection Example
 
 @itemize
 @item
+Tone map HDR10 or Dolby Vision profile 5 (after @code{dovi_reshape}) to SDR
+with the BT.2408 Hable curve, then convert to limited range BT.709 YUV
+@example
+format=p010,hwupload,tonemap_vaapi=tonemap=bt2408_hable,hwdownload,format=rgba,scale=out_color_matrix=bt709:out_range=tv,format=yuv420p
+@end example
+@item
 Convert HDR(HDR10) video to bt2020-transfer-characteristic p010 format
 @example
 tonemap_vaapi=format=p010:t=bt2020-10
